Hi,

Six fixes for the ibmveth driver. They apply to net-next as is and
do not depend on the two open() error-path fixes recently applied to
net (af0524bf4ce1, 84bec0bf0352); patch 3 explains how it relates to
them. Several of the bugs can take the partition down with no
recovery short of a reboot; the others are memory corruption or a
NULL dereference.

They target net-next rather than net: the triggers are rare (an
open() failure during a direct reopen, PHYP returning a bad
correlator, netconsole during a reconfiguration or under TX
contention, a bad RX slot during remove) and there are no field
reports. All six carry Fixes: tags and are suitable for stable once
merged; I can repost them against net if you prefer.

Patches 3, 5 and 6 were requested by the netdev AI review of v7 of
the ibmveth multi-queue RX series, which asked for these fixes to be
split out of it with Fixes: tags:
https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/cover.1790319558.git.mmc@linux.ibm.com/
Patches 1, 2 and 4 came out of the follow-up review of the same code.

Patch 1 enables NAPI in open() only once the RX resources exist.
netpoll polls NAPI during the driver's direct close()/open() pairs,
where its dev_lock is not held, and could replenish pools that were
not allocated yet.

Patch 2 removes ndo_poll_controller. It ran replenish from netpoll
outside NAPI with no lock, racing NAPI's replenish on the same pool,
so a free slot could be posted to PHYP twice. The callback is
unnecessary since netpoll polls NAPI itself, as was done for
ibmvnic.

Patch 3 stops a second close() after a failed direct reopen.
change_mtu, the pool sysfs store, set_csum and set_tso close and
reopen the device directly; if that open() fails, IFF_UP stays set
and the next ndo_stop napi_disable()s an already-disabled NAPI with
RTNL held. The hang is deterministic once open() has failed, and it
also blocks shutdown.

Patch 4 disables the reset work before unregister in remove(), so a
reset queued from NAPI in between cannot run on a freed adapter.
Patch 5 makes that window reachable.

Patch 5 makes poll step past a bad RX slot. Since 2c91e2319ed9
turned the correlator BUG_ON()s into WARN_ON() plus a reset, poll
breaks out without advancing the ring and restarts on the same slot
forever. The reset it schedules is queued on the stuck CPU and never
runs, and the CPU stalls RCU. The WARN_ON()s on PHYP-supplied data
become a ratelimited error.

Patch 6 rejects correlators that name an inactive buffer pool, which
passed the size check and dereferenced a NULL skbuff array in
softirq.

Each commit message says how the bug was found and how the fix was
tested. In short: the ibmveth KUnit suite on qemu pseries (ppc64le)
passes, and the new cases in patches 5 and 6 fail on the unfixed
driver; @@HW-COVER: LPAR model/firmware and what was run@@.

